      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose is above the maximum for metformin.\n\n- **Ordered:** 1700 mg three times daily = 5100 mg/day\n- **Maximum for immediate-release metformin:** 2550 mg/day (commonly 850 mg TID or 1000 mg BID)\n- **Maximum for extended-release metformin:** 2000 mg/day\n- **Standard tablet strengths:** 500, 850, and 1000 mg. 1700 mg is not a standard single tablet, so it may be two 850 mg tablets, which would be a dose error if unintended.\n\nSome possible intended orders:\n1. Metformin 850 mg PO TID with meals (2550 mg/day, IR maximum)\n2. Metformin 1000 mg PO BID with meals (2000 mg/day)\n3. Metformin 500 mg PO TID with meals (1500 mg/day, a lower starting or titration dose)\n4. Metformin ER 1000 mg PO with the evening meal, or 500 mg with meals, to reach up to 2000 mg/day\n\nPlease confirm the intended dose, formulation (IR or ER), and frequency, and I'll enter it. If 1700 mg TID was intended after a deliberate review, please confirm that too. I would still recommend checking it against the prescriber's plan and the pharmacy's dose-range guidance first."
      }
